@node spectrum-analyzer Plugin Parameters
@section Parameters

This plugin has no user-tunable parameters.


@strong{Structural parameters} (Num Bins) require rebuilding the plugin when changed. Other parameters update in real-time with zero dropout.

@node spectrum-analyzer Plugin Developer Guide
@section Developer Guide

Tap-style analyser. Audio is windowed (Hann by default) and fed through an FFT; magnitudes are smoothed across frames and passed to the UI through a lock-free SPSC channel. No processing is applied to the audio signal.

@subsubheading Parameter wiring

All parameters reach the audio thread through the host's @code{rebuild_cached_parameters} / @code{set_parameter} / @code{get_parameter} triad. Structural parameters (marked in the notes below) trigger a rebuild; the rest update in real time with zero dropouts.

@subsubheading Source

The @code{spectrum-analyzer} plugin does not have a dedicated crate at the time of writing; its implementation lives under @file{crates/sotf-plugins/crates/sotf-host/} or one of the multi-component crates. Search the workspace for the plugin type key @code{"spectrum-analyzer"} to locate it.

Run the unit tests with @code{cargo test -p sotf-plugin-spectrum-analyzer}.

